From cf2c0ec35f59a76a7d0fd3d9e8dc7e377c240fae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Wakely <jwakely@redhat.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:59:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] libstdc++: Do not include <bits/indirect.h> for freestanding
 [PR127476]

This header is not installed for freestanding builds, so we should not
try to include it.

We could consider making std::indirect and std::polymorphic available
for freestanding, but that would be more effort as it requires
installing <bits/new_allocator.h> and other headers.

libstdc++-v3/ChangeLog:

	PR libstdc++/127476
	* include/std/memory [!_GLIBCXX_HOSTED]: Do not include
	bits/indirect.h.

(cherry picked from commit 7e5fe1837c79233a9cdb2fdef655f82f8cabdafb)
---
 libstdc++-v3/include/std/memory | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libstdc++-v3/include/std/memory b/libstdc++-v3/include/std/memory
index cbe9f5ad2007..f83745081590 100644
--- a/libstdc++-v3/include/std/memory
+++ b/libstdc++-v3/include/std/memory
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
 #  include <bits/out_ptr.h>
 #endif
 
-#if __cplusplus > 202302L
+#if __cplusplus > 202302L && _GLIBCXX_HOSTED
 #  include <bits/indirect.h>
 #endif
 
